content.text:
I have everything needed. Here is the complete investigation report.

---

# NxCloud Feature — Pattern Investigation

All paths absolute. Root: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud`

## 1. Marketing Page Pattern

There are **two** marketing page shapes in this repo. Pick based on how bespoke you want NxCloud to be.

### Option A — `UseCaseLanding` shell (what `nextcloud-hosting/page.tsx` uses)

This is the fastest path: a server component that fetches plans and passes a big `content` object into a shared shell. The whole page (hero, intro, why-cards, steps, pricing grid, FAQ, related, CTA) is rendered for you.

File: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/(marketing)/nextcloud-hosting/page.tsx`

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { UseCaseLanding, type UseCaseContent } from "@/components/marketing/UseCaseLanding";

export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";

const APP_URL = process.env.APP_URL ?? "https://nxeon.cloud";

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "Nextcloud Hosting — Self-Hosted Cloud Storage VPS",
  description: "...",
  alternates: { canonical: "/nextcloud-hosting" },
  openGraph: { type: "article", title: "...", description: "...", url: `${APP_URL}/nextcloud-hosting` },
};

const content: UseCaseContent = { eyebrow, title, highlight, sub, intro:[...], whyTitle, why:[...], steps:[...], specNote, faq:[...], related:[...] };

export default async function NextcloudHostingPage() {
  const plans = await db.plan.findMany({ where: { active: true }, orderBy: { sortOrder: "asc" } });
  return <UseCaseLanding content={content} plans={plans} />;
}
```

The `UseCaseContent` type (from `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/marketing/UseCaseLanding.tsx`) is your entire authoring surface:

```ts
export type UseCaseContent = {
  eyebrow: string;
  title: string;      // H1 lead-in (plain)
  highlight: string;  // gradient highlight word appended to title
  sub: string;
  intro: string[];    // 1–3 paragraphs
  whyTitle: string;
  why: { title: string; body: string }[];
  steps: { title: string; body: string }[];
  specNote?: string;
  faq: { q: string; a: string }[];
  related?: { label: string; href: string }[];
};
```

The shell hardcodes the hero CTAs to `Deploy now → /register` and `See pricing → #pricing`, renders `<PricingGrid plans={plans} />`, and injects `FaqJsonLd` + `ProductJsonLd`. Note it consumes `PlanCard[]` from `./PricingGrid` and expects `db.plan` records (the generic VPS plans), not `db.hostingPlan`.

### Option B — Hand-built page (what `web-hosting/page.tsx` uses) — recommended if NxCloud is a first-class product

This composes the shared primitives directly, giving you full control over sections. This is the pattern to clone for a polished, unique product page.

File: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/(marketing)/web-hosting/page.tsx`

Import structure:

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import Link from "next/link";
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { Section, SectionTitle, PageHero } from "@/components/marketing/primitives";
import { FeatureCard, CtaBand } from "@/components/marketing/sections";
import { Reveal } from "@/components/marketing/Reveal";
import { FaqJsonLd } from "@/components/marketing/StructuredData";
import { IconGlobe, IconShield, IconBolt, IconDisk, IconMail, IconGauge, IconApps, IconCheck } from "@/components/marketing/icons";
import { currentPromo } from "@/lib/promotions";
import { PromoBadge } from "@/components/marketing/PromoBadge";

export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
export const metadata: Metadata = { title: "Web Hosting", description: "..." };
```

Structure of the page body:
- `<PageHero eyebrow title highlight sub primary={{label,href}} secondary={{label,href}} />` — the standard hero (from `primitives.tsx`).
- Repeated `<Section tone="base|panel|deep|light">` bands, each with `<SectionTitle eyebrow title sub />`.
- Feature grid: `<div className="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">` of `<FeatureCard icon={<IconBolt/>} title="…" delay={0.05}>body</FeatureCard>`.
- Plan cards fetched from DB and mapped:

```tsx
const plans = await db.hostingPlan.findMany({ where: { active: true }, orderBy: { sortOrder: "asc" } });
// ...
{plans.map((p, i) => (
  <Reveal key={p.id} delay={i * 0.05} className="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-navy-850/60 p-6">
    <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{p.name}</h3>
    <p className="mt-1 text-3xl font-bold text-white">{money(p.priceCents)}<span className="text-sm font-normal text-slate-400">/mo</span></p>
    <ul className="mt-4 flex-1 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-300"><li>…</li></ul>
    <Link href="/dashboard/hosting" className="btn-primary mt-6 text-center">Get started</Link>
  </Reveal>
))}
```

- Empty-state guard: `{plans.length === 0 ? <Reveal>…coming soon…</Reveal> : (<grid/>)}`.
- FAQ cards, then a final `<Section><CtaBand /></Section>`.
- `money` helper defined inline: `const money = (c: number) => \`$${(c / 100).toFixed(2)}\`;`

### Shared marketing primitives (the reuse layer)

`/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/marketing/primitives.tsx`:
- `Section({ children, tone="base"|"panel"|"deep"|"light", size="sm"|"md"|"lg", id, className })` — wraps content in `<div className="rail">`; tone maps to `tone-panel`/`tone-deep`/`tone-light` classes.
- `Eyebrow({ children, pill })` — `eyebrow` / `eyebrow-pill` class.
- `SectionTitle({ eyebrow, title, sub, align="center"|"left" })` — h2 uses `text-[var(--fg)]`, sub uses `text-[var(--fg-muted)]`.
- `PageHero({ eyebrow, title, highlight, sub, primary, secondary, visual, children })` — renders `.hero-aura` glow, `<span className="grad-text">{highlight}</span>`, and `btn-primary`/`btn-secondary` CTAs.

`/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/marketing/sections.tsx`:
- `FeatureCard({ icon, title, children, delay })` — icon sits in a `bg-gradient-to-br from-accent-blue/20 to-brand-500/20 ... text-brand-300` chip, card uses `card card-hover group`.
- `CtaBand()` — the sitewide closing CTA (radial navy/violet/blue glow, `grad-text`, register + pricing buttons). Reused on 22 pages.
- `SectionHeading`, `TrustBadges` also here.

Icons: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/marketing/icons.tsx` (e.g. `IconGlobe, IconShield, IconBolt, IconDisk, IconMail, IconGauge, IconApps, IconCheck, IconArrow` — all take an optional `size` prop).

### Brand colors / CSS variables (design system)

Defined in `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/globals.css` under `@theme` (Tailwind v4, no `tailwind.config` — colors are CSS vars):

```css
--color-brand-400: #8a70fb;  /* violet — the signature accent */
--color-brand-500: #6f47f5;
--color-brand-300: #a89aff;
--color-navy-950: #060a14;   /* page bg */
--color-navy-900: #0a101f;
--color-navy-850: #0d1526;   /* card surfaces */
--color-accent-blue: #3b82f6;
--color-accent-cyan: #22d3ee;
```

Key utility classes (also in globals.css):
- `.card` → `rounded-2xl border border-white/[0.06] bg-navy-900/70 p-6 backdrop-blur-md` + inset shadow.
- `.card-hover` → `hover:border-brand-500/30 hover:bg-navy-850/80`.
- `.grad-text` → `bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-blue via-brand-400 to-brand-500 bg-clip-text text-transparent` (the navy→cyan/blue→violet brand gradient).
- `.btn-primary` → `bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-blue to-brand-500 text-white` + violet glow shadow.
- `.btn-secondary` → bordered white/glass.
- `--fg` / `--fg-muted` swap per tone (white/slate-400 on dark, slate-900/slate-600 on `.tone-light`).
- `.rail`, `.hero-aura`, `.tone-panel/.tone-deep/.tone-light`, `.page-title`, `.section-label`.

Tailwind color usage in JSX: `brand-500`, `brand-400`, `brand-300/200`, `navy-850/900/950`, `accent-blue`, `accent-cyan`, plus `emerald-*` (success), `red-*`, `amber-*`, `slate-300/400/500`.

**Recommendation:** clone `web-hosting/page.tsx` into `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/(marketing)/nxcloud/page.tsx`, add `alternates: { canonical: "/nxcloud" }` + `openGraph` like the nextcloud-hosting page, and point plan-card CTAs at `/dashboard/nxcloud`.

---

## 2. Dashboard Layout Nav

File: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/dashboard/layout.tsx`

Nav is a `NavSection[]` array (type from `@/components/portal/Shell`). To add an **NxCloud** tab, add an item to the existing **Compute** section (lines 30–40):

```tsx
{
  label: "Compute",
  items: [
    { label: "Deploy", href: "/dashboard/deploy", icon: "rocket" },
    { label: "Servers", href: "/dashboard/servers", icon: "server" },
    { label: "Shared Hosting", href: "/dashboard/hosting", icon: "globe" },
    { label: "NxCloud", href: "/dashboard/nxcloud", icon: "folder" },  // <-- add
    { label: "Game Servers", href: "/dashboard/games", icon: "server" },
    { label: "Migration Center", href: "/dashboard/migrate", icon: "rocket" },
    { label: "Volumes", href: "/dashboard/volumes", icon: "db" },
  ],
},
```

Types (`/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/portal/Shell.tsx`):
```ts
export type NavItem = { label: string; href: string; icon?: string; badge?: number; /* +children */ };
export type NavSection = { label?: string; items: NavItem[] };
```

Valid `icon` keys (the `icons` map in Shell.tsx): `home, server, rocket, globe, folder, card, chat, cog, pulse, users, shield, bolt, chart, dollar, queue`. (Note: line 39 uses `"db"` which is not in that list, so it falls back to `icons.folder` — `folder` or `server` is the safe pick for NxCloud, a storage product.)

**Optional feature flag:** if you want NxCloud gated behind a setting until launch, add an entry to the `FEATURE_HREF` map (lines 12–24) and a matching flag in the `flags` object (lines 117–125):
```tsx
const FEATURE_HREF = { /* ... */ "/dashboard/nxcloud": "feature_nxcloud" };
// and:
feature_nxcloud: await getSettingBool("feature_nxcloud", false),
```
The layout auto-filters items whose flag is off and drops empty sections.

---

## 3. Dashboard Product Tab Pattern

Server page: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/dashboard/hosting/page.tsx`

```tsx
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { requireUser } from "@/lib/auth";
import { listHostingAccounts } from "@/lib/actions-hosting";
import { HostingClient } from "@/components/customer/HostingClient";

export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";

export default async function HostingPage() {
  await requireUser();  // <-- auth gate
  const [plans, accounts] = await Promise.all([
    db.hostingPlan.findMany({ where: { active: true }, orderBy: { sortOrder: "asc" } }),
    listHostingAccounts(),  // server action that queries by the current user internally
  ]);
  const planViews = plans.map((p) => ({ id: p.id, name: p.name, priceCents: p.priceCents, /* ...plain fields... */ }));
  return <HostingClient plans={planViews} accounts={accounts} />;
}
```

**Auth pattern:** import `requireUser` from `@/lib/auth`. Exact signatures (`/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/lib/auth.ts`):
- `requireUser(): Promise<User>` — throws `"UNAUTHORIZED"` if no session (used in dashboard *pages*, since the dashboard `layout.tsx` already redirected).
- `currentUser()` — cached, returns `User | null` (respects impersonation); used in the layout.
- `realUser()` — cached, ignores impersonation.

The per-user DB query lives inside the server action `listHostingAccounts()` in `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/lib/actions-hosting.ts` (it calls `requireUser()` then filters `where: { userId: user.id }` and returns a `HostingAccountView[]` DTO). Clone this into an `actions-nxcloud.ts` with `listNxcloudInstances()`.

**List + empty state + status badges** live in the client component `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/customer/HostingClient.tsx` (`"use client"`):

```tsx
import { Badge, EmptyState, StatusDot, fmtMoney } from "@/components/ui/primitives";

{accounts.length > 0 ? (
  <div className="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {accounts.map((a) => <AccountCard key={a.id} a={a} onRetry={() => retry(a.id)} />)}
  </div>
) : (
  <EmptyState title="No hosting accounts yet" sub="Pick a plan below…" />
)}
```

`AccountCard` renders `<StatusDot status={a.status} />`, storage/quota chips, `<Badge tone="green">HTTPS</Badge>`, wraps in a `<Link href={\`/dashboard/hosting/${a.id}\`} className="card card-hover block">`, and special-cases `status === "FAILED"` with an inline retry.

**Shared UI primitives** (`/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/ui/primitives.tsx`):
- `StatusDot({ status, label })` — colored pulsing dot; has built-in mappings for `RUNNING/ACTIVE/PENDING/PROVISIONING/FAILED/SUSPENDED/...` (add any new NxCloud status strings to the `statusColors` map there, else it falls back to grey `STOPPED`).
- `Badge({ children, tone: "brand"|"green"|"red"|"amber"|"slate" })`.
- `EmptyState({ title, sub?, action? })`.
- `fmtMoney(cents)`, `fmtBytes(b)`, `timeAgo(d)`, `PageHeader`, `StatCard`, `ComingSoon`.

Create `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/dashboard/nxcloud/page.tsx` (server, `requireUser()` + parallel DB fetch) delegating to a `components/customer/NxcloudClient.tsx`.

---

## 4. Admin Visibility Pattern

Two good reference files:

### Simple wrapper: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/admin/hosting/page.tsx`
```tsx
import { requireArea } from "@/lib/rbac";
import { PageHeader } from "@/components/ui/primitives";
import { adminListHostingInfra, adminListHostingAccounts } from "@/lib/actions-hosting";
import { HostingInfra } from "@/components/admin/HostingInfra";
import { HostingAccountsAdmin } from "@/components/admin/HostingAccountsAdmin";

export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";

export default async function AdminHostingPage() {
  await requireArea("fleet");   // <-- role guard
  const [{ plans, nodes }, accounts] = await Promise.all([adminListHostingInfra(), adminListHostingAccounts()]);
  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      <PageHeader title="Web Hosting" sub="..." />
      <HostingAccountsAdmin accounts={accounts} />
      <HostingInfra plans={plans} nodes={nodes} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Full table render: `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/admin/servers/page.tsx`
```tsx
import Link from "next/link";
import { requireArea } from "@/lib/rbac";
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { PageHeader, StatusDot, Badge, fmtMoney } from "@/components/ui/primitives";

export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";

export default async function AdminServers({ searchParams }: { searchParams: Promise<{ status?: string }> }) {
  await requireArea("fleet");
  const [servers, counts] = await Promise.all([
    db.server.findMany({ include: { user: { select: { id: true, email: true } }, plan: { select: { name: true, priceCents: true } } }, orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" } }),
    db.server.groupBy({ by: ["status"], _count: true }),
  ]);
  // renders a filterable table with StatusDot / Badge / fmtMoney cells
}
```

**Auth guard — `requireArea` (RBAC) is the admin pattern, not `requireAdmin`.** From `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/lib/rbac.ts`:

```ts
export type Area = "overview"|"analytics"|"clients"|"support"|"fleet"|"billing"|"platform";
export const AREA_ROLES: Record<Area, Role[]> = {
  fleet: ["ADMIN"],  // ADMIN-only (servers, hosting, nodes, provisioning all use "fleet")
  clients: ["SUPPORT","ADMIN"], support: ["SUPPORT","ADMIN"], billing: ["BILLING","ADMIN"], platform: ["ADMIN"], /* ... */
};
export async function requireArea(area: Area): Promise<User> {
  const user = await realUser();
  if (!user) redirect("/login");
  if (!isStaff(user.role)) redirect("/dashboard");
  if (!canAccess(user.role, area)) redirect("/admin");
  return user;
}
```

For NxCloud (an infrastructure/compute product) use `await requireArea("fleet")` — same as hosting/servers, restricting to `ADMIN`. Also register the route in the `HREF_AREA` map in `rbac.ts` so the admin nav and hand-typed-URL guard agree:

```ts
const HREF_AREA: Record<string, Area> = { /* ... */ "/admin/nxcloud": "fleet" };
```

(There is also a blunt `requireAdmin()` in `@/lib/auth.ts` that throws `"FORBIDDEN"` for non-ADMIN — but the admin *pages* consistently use `requireArea`, which redirects instead of throwing. Match the surrounding pages: use `requireArea`.)

Admin list/table components live in `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/admin/` (e.g. `HostingAccountsAdmin.tsx`, `HostingInfra.tsx`) and admin data-fetching server actions in `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/lib/actions-hosting.ts` (`adminListHostingAccounts`, `adminListHostingInfra`). Mirror these as `components/admin/NxcloudAdmin.tsx` + `adminListNxcloud*()`.

---

### Files to create (summary)
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/(marketing)/nxcloud/page.tsx` (clone `web-hosting/page.tsx`)
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/dashboard/nxcloud/page.tsx` + `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/customer/NxcloudClient.tsx`
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/admin/nxcloud/page.tsx` + `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/admin/NxcloudAdmin.tsx`
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/lib/actions-nxcloud.ts` (customer + admin server actions)

### Files to edit
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/app/dashboard/layout.tsx` — add nav item to Compute section
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/lib/rbac.ts` — add `"/admin/nxcloud": "fleet"` to `HREF_AREA`
- `/opt/nxeon-wt-nxcloud/components/ui/primitives.tsx` — add any new NxCloud status strings to the `statusColors` map in `StatusDot`

One note that may bite you: the two marketing pages read from **different plan tables** — `UseCaseLanding` expects `db.plan` (VPS plans → `PlanCard`), while `web-hosting` uses `db.hostingPlan`. Decide which plan model NxCloud instances bill against before wiring the pricing grid.
